WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
London, the 1950s.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.260
Bus drivers sat at the wheel all day.

3
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.760
Conductors climbed the
stairs, again and again.

4
00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.160
The drivers had more heart disease.

5
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.640
Too little exercise is linked to obesity,

6
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.160
cardiovascular disease
and type 2 diabetes.

7
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.390
But some athletes train
for hours every day.

8
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.190
So can doing far more exercise
ever start to harm you?

9
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.710
In this mission, you'll see surgeons repair
a torn knee through two or three small

10
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.650
cuts, with a camera inside the joint.

11
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.650
Then you'll see how a
running blade returns energy,

12
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.160
and weigh the arguments over drugs
that build muscle or boost endurance.

13
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:43.820
Your mission: find out whether doing
far more exercise can ever start to harm

14
00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:44.200
you.
